---
import DocLayout from "../../layouts/DocLayout.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<DocLayout
  title="Operator’s overview"
  eyebrow="SECTION 01 / ORIENTATION"
  description="Lanyard gives every shell, multiplexer, SSH client, and Git process one durable SSH agent address while routing each request to the agents that are actually available."
>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>The assignment</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>SSH_AUTH_SOCK</code> once—to Lanyard’s stable socket—and stop carrying
      temporary agent paths across session boundaries. Lanyard discovers forwarded
      OpenSSH agents, accepts explicit registrations, and keeps a static local agent
      such as 1Password in reserve.
    </p>
    <div class="note">
      <strong>DEFAULT SOCKET</strong><code
        >$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/lanyard-ssh-agent/agent.sock</code
      >
    </div>
    <h2>What it handles</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Normal SSH public-key authentication.</li><li>
        Git commit and tag signing with <code>gpg.format = ssh</code>.
      </li><li>
        Sessions that outlive the forwarded agent which created them.
      </li><li>
        Multiple simultaneous remote logins, without manual socket surgery.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <h2>What it does not do</h2>
    <p>
      Lanyard is not an agent, keychain, secret store, or forwarding transport.
      It cannot unlock 1Password and it never reads private key material. It is
      a deliberately read-only protocol router.
    </p>
    <div class="next-links">
      <a href={`${base}docs/quick-start/`}>NEXT / QUICK START →</a><a
        href={`${base}docs/architecture/`}>SEE / ARCHITECTURE →</a
      >
    </div>
  </div>
</DocLayout>
